# Testing is mandatory

Any new or changed **functionality** must include automated tests in the same change.

## Policy

- No feature, bug fix, or behavior change without tests that would fail if the change were reverted
- Prefer the **test pyramid**: many unit → fewer integration → very few e2e
- Balance with **SMURF** (Google): Speed, Maintainability, Utilization, Reliability, Fidelity — do not optimize only for count of tests
- Avoid the **ice-cream cone**: lots of slow e2e and almost no unit tests

## Where tests live

```text
tests/
├── unit/           # Isolated pure logic (no network, no real LLM)
├── integration/    # API / component boundaries (TestClient, mocked LLM)
└── e2e/            # Critical full-path flows (real HTTP against running app/container)
```

## Mapping for this project

| Change | Minimum tests |
|---|---|
| Schema / validation | `tests/unit/` |
| CAG loader / prompt builders | `tests/unit/` |
| Router + service wiring | `tests/integration/` (LLM mocked) |
| Happy-path estimate + health | one thin `tests/e2e/` or CI container smoke |

## Do not

- Merge untested behavior “to add tests later”
- Call real OpenAI/Anthropic in unit or default CI (use fakes/mocks)
- Duplicate the same assertion at every pyramid layer
